<title>LITHUANIA: YIELDS FALL ON 28-DAY T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELDS FALL ON 28-DAY T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on 28-day Lithuanian</p>
<p>Treasury bills at Monday's auction and all of the 30 million</p>
<p>litas issue was sold as it was oversubscribed, the country's</p>
<p>central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield was 7.87 percent, down from the 8.46</p>
<p>percent offered at the last auction for 28-day paper on April</p>
<p>22.</p>
<p>The settlement date is June 5 and the bills mature on July</p>
<p>3.</p>
<p>All amounts in millions of litas unless otherwise</p>
<p>specified.</p>
<p>SOLD  DEMAND  MATURITY  MIN/MAX YIELD (PCT)  AV YIELD  LAST</p>
<p>30    89.546  28 days   7.20/8.23		  7.87    8.46</p>
<p>-- Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
</text>
